                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Once the game explains how to make the motion less nauseating, I can admit its pretty good. I personally don't like the genre, but I can acknowledge it's well made.\n\nIt's hard. Most of the difficulty comes from a disorienting angle and not the tightest controls. This is all done intentionally. It's sort of like a 2d Mario Galaxy, but difficult as fudge. There's even 3 fish to collect in each stage which upon collecting a certain amount, unlocks the next area. The final stage in each area is tough, but beating it unlocks you a new octopus, each with a different kind of ability.\nAt least, that's what I assume, as I only completed the first area, for the difficulty really ramps up in the second area.\n\nSure, it's unique and creative and decent overall, but it's main gimmick that the gameplay is centered on just makes it not fun to play. The disorientation and loose controls make you feel not in control, which is the biggest turn off for me when it comes to games. Coupled with the fact that I loathe games that make you try the same sections over and over again, I lost interest pretty quickly.\n\nIf the trailer looks appealing to you, and your into this genre, chances are you'll enjoy it.",
